IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`
IMPORT `ssc3-a-s43-s44`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, ss 51 to 55 (part ssc3).
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- Category B retirement pension for those who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010 and were widowed (s 51);
-- the gender-change rules (s 51ZA); the top-up of a Category A pension from a Category B one (ss 51A and 52);
-- election (s 54); deferred entitlement (s 55). Sections 49, 50 and 53 are blank in this text.
--
-- "over pensionable age at the time of the death": section 173(a) of this Act says a person "is over or under a
-- particular age if he has or, as the case may be, has not attained that age". The core gives the day a person attains
-- pensionable age, so "over pensionable age at a time" is encoded as that day being on or before the time.
--
-- The weekly rates of the basic and additional pensions come from sections 44 to 45AA (ssc3-a and ssc3-c); the caller
-- supplies them, as for section 48B (ssc3-d), and the amounts that Schedules 4 and 5 give arrive as inputs.

§ `Part II: retirement pensions, supplemental sections`

§§ `Section 51: Category B retirement pension for widows, widowers and surviving civil partners who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010`

-- (3): the relevant contribution condition for a spouse: paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 where the spouse attained pensionable
-- age before 6 April 2010, paragraph 5A where on or after that date.
-- src:1615 | (3) In subsection (1)(c) “the relevant contribution condition” means—
-- src:1616 | (a) in a case where the spouse attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010, the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3, and
-- src:1617 | (b) in a case where the spouse attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2010, the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 51(3) (src:1615-1617)
GIVEN spouse IS A Person
GIVETH A `s 44(1A) Contribution test`
`s 51(3) the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
    IF spouse's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
    THEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
    ELSE `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`

-- (5): the same for a deceased civil partner.
-- src:1622 | (5) In subsection (4)(c) “the relevant contribution condition” means—
-- src:1623 | (a) in a case where the deceased civil partner attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010, the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3, and
-- src:1624 | (b) in a case where the deceased civil partner attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2010, the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 51(5) (src:1622-1624)
GIVEN `deceased civil partner` IS A Person
GIVETH A `s 44(1A) Contribution test`
`s 51(5) the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
    IF `deceased civil partner`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
    THEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
    ELSE `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`

-- (2): subsection (1) does not confer a right on (a) a woman whose husband has died or (b) a man whose wife died before
-- 6 April 1979. Section 51ZA(4) adds a third case, below.
-- src:1612 | (2) But subsection (1) does not confer a right to a Category B retirement pension on—
-- src:1613 | (a) a woman whose husband has died, or
-- src:1614 | (b) a man whose wife died before 6 April 1979.
@ref s 51(2) (src:1612-1614)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      spouse IS A Person
      `the spouse died on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF pensioner's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND spouse's `sex` EQUALS Man THEN TRUE
        IF pensioner's `sex` EQUALS Man AND spouse's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND `the spouse died on` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1979) THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is stated for "(a) a woman whose husband has died, or (b) a man whose wife died before 6 April 1979" and for no one else (a closed list)

-- (4) of section 51ZA: subsection 51(1) does not confer a right on a woman whose dead spouse was, at the time of
-- death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and the marriage subsisted before it was issued.
-- src:1649 | (4) Section 51(1) does not confer a right to a Category B retirement pension on a woman if—
-- src:1650 | (a) her dead spouse was, at the time of death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004, and
-- src:1651 | (b) the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued.
@ref s 51ZA(4) (src:1649-1651)
GIVEN woman IS A Person
      `her dead spouse was at the time of death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51ZA(4) section 51(1) does not confer a right on the woman` MEANS
    woman's `sex` EQUALS Woman
    AND `her dead spouse was at the time of death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004`
    AND `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 51(1) does not confer a right ... on a woman if (a) ... and (b) ..." -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))

-- (1): a person whose spouse died while they were married is entitled to a Category B retirement pension if (a) they were
-- both over pensionable age at the time of the death, (b) the pensioner attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010 and
-- (c) the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition (3). Subsections (2) and 51ZA(4) are bars on (1).
-- src:1608 | (1) A person (“the pensioner”) whose spouse died while they were married is entitled to a Category B retirement pension if—
-- src:1609 | (a) they were both over pensionable age at the time of the death,
-- src:1610 | (b) the pensioner attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010, and
-- src:1611 | (c) the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition.
@ref s 51(1) (src:1608-1611)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      spouse IS A Person
      `the spouse died on` IS A DATE
      `the spouse died while they were married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `her dead spouse was at the time of death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (\"the pensioner\") whose spouse died while they were married is entitled to a Category B retirement pension if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a)); and "But subsection (1) does not confer a right" (s 51(2)) and "Section 51(1) does not confer a right" (s 51ZA(4))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (NOT (`s 51(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` pensioner spouse `the spouse died on`))
          , JUST (NOT (`s 51ZA(4) section 51(1) does not confer a right on the woman` pensioner `her dead spouse was at the time of death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued`))
          , JUST `the spouse died while they were married`
          , JUST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST `the spouse died on`)
          , JUST (spouse's `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST `the spouse died on`)
          , JUST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010))
          , `the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition`)
    WHERE
        `the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 51(3) the relevant contribution condition` spouse
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`

-- (4): a person whose civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other is entitled to a Category B
-- retirement pension if (a) they were both over pensionable age at the time of the death, (b) the pensioner attained
-- pensionable age before 6 April 2010 and (c) the deceased civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition (5).
-- src:1618 | (4) A person (“the pensioner”) whose civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other is entitled to a Category B retirement pension if—
-- src:1619 | (a) they were both over pensionable age at the time of the death,
-- src:1620 | (b) the pensioner attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010, and
-- src:1621 | (c) the deceased civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition.
@ref s 51(4) (src:1618-1621)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `deceased civil partner` IS A Person
      `the civil partner died on` IS A DATE
      `the civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (\"the pensioner\") whose civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other is entitled to a Category B retirement pension if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST `the civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other`
          , JUST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST `the civil partner died on`)
          , JUST (`deceased civil partner`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST `the civil partner died on`)
          , JUST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010))
          , `the deceased civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition`)
    WHERE
        `the deceased civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 51(5) the relevant contribution condition` `deceased civil partner`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`

-- (6): the weekly rate is determined under ss 44 to 45AA and Schedules 4A and 4B as for a Category A retirement
-- pension, taking references to the pensioner as references to the spouse or deceased civil partner.
-- src:1625 | (6) The weekly rate of a person's Category B retirement pension under this section is to be determined in accordance with sections 44 to 45AA and Schedules 4A and 4B as they apply in the case of a Category A retirement pension taking references in those sections to the pensioner as references to the spouse or deceased civil partner.
@ref s 51(6) (src:1625)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `spouse or deceased civil partner` IS A Person
      `the rate is that of a Category B retirement pension under section 51` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Person
`s 51(6) the person to whom a reference to the pensioner is taken to refer` MEANS
    IF `the rate is that of a Category B retirement pension under section 51`
    THEN JUST `spouse or deceased civil partner`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reading is made for "a person's Category B retirement pension under this section"

-- (7): any amount of additional pension falling to be calculated under (6) is halved in the case of (a) a man whose wife
-- dies after 5 October 2002, (b) a surviving party to a marriage of a same sex couple, or (c) a surviving civil partner.
-- Outside those cases the amount stands as determined under (6) (marginal reading (c) in NOTES.md).
-- src:1626 | (7) But in the case of—
-- src:1627 | (a) a man whose wife dies after 5 October 2002,
-- src:1628 | (b) a surviving party to a marriage of a same sex couple, or
-- src:1629 | (c) a surviving civil partner,
-- src:1630 | any amount of additional pension falling to be calculated under subsection (6) is to be halved.
@ref s 51(7) (src:1626-1630)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      spouse IS A Person
      `the spouse died on` IS A DATE
      `the pensioner is a surviving civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of additional pension calculated under subsection (6) in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount of additional pension calculated under subsection (6) in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        IF `a man whose wife dies after 5 October 2002` OR `a surviving party to a marriage of a same sex couple` OR `the pensioner is a surviving civil partner`
        THEN JUST (amount DIVIDED BY 2)
        ELSE JUST amount  -- unmodified, not a "no": the halving is made "in the case of" (a), (b) or (c); outside them the amount stands (marginal reading (c) in NOTES.md)
    WHERE
        `a man whose wife dies after 5 October 2002` MEANS
            pensioner's `sex` EQUALS Man AND spouse's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND `the spouse died on` GREATER THAN (Date 5 10 2002)
        `a surviving party to a marriage of a same sex couple` MEANS
            pensioner's `sex` EQUALS spouse's `sex`

-- (6): the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension is the basic pension plus the additional pension after (7).
-- src:1625 | (6) The weekly rate of a person's Category B retirement pension under this section is to be determined in accordance with sections 44 to 45AA and Schedules 4A and 4B as they apply in the case of a Category A retirement pension taking references in those sections to the pensioner as references to the spouse or deceased civil partner.
@ref s 51(6), the rate (src:1625)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the basic pension determined as for a Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 51(6) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper sum of`
        (LIST
            `the weekly rate of the basic pension determined as for a Category A retirement pension in pounds`
          , `the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds`)

-- (8): no account of earnings factors of the spouse or deceased civil partner for the tax year beginning 6 April 2016
-- or any later tax year.
-- src:1631 | (8) For the purposes of any provision of this Act as it applies in relation to this section, no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the spouse or deceased civil partner for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year.
@ref s 51(8) (src:1631)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(8) the earnings factor of the spouse or deceased civil partner for the tax year is taken into account` MEANS
    IF year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 2016
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the spouse or deceased civil partner for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): earlier years are left to the other provisions

-- (9): entitlement begins on the day the conditions are satisfied and continues throughout the person's life.
-- src:1632 | (9) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person becomes entitled to a Category B retirement pension under this section on the day on which the conditions of entitlement become satisfied and the entitlement continues throughout the person's life.
@ref s 51(9) (src:1632)
GIVEN `the day the conditions of entitlement become satisfied` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      `the date of the person's death` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(9) the entitlement to a Category B retirement pension under section 51 is running on the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `the day the conditions of entitlement become satisfied`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a person "becomes entitled ... on the day on which the conditions of entitlement become satisfied"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the date of the person's death`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST death THEN IF day AT MOST death THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement "continues throughout the person's life"

-- (11) and (12): where the spouse or civil partner attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016 and died after
-- attaining it, the additional pension is increased by the percentage by which it would have increased under orders
-- under section 150 of the Administration Act from the date pensionable age was reached to the death. The percentage
-- arrives as an input; it is applied as a multiplier of (1 + the percentage / 100) (fork F6, see NOTES.md).
-- src:1634 | (11) Subsection (12) applies in the case of a pensioner whose spouse or civil partner—
-- src:1635 | (a) attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1636 | (b) died after attaining pensionable age.
-- src:1637 | (12) Where this subsection applies, the amount determined in accordance with this section as the weekly rate of the additional pension payable to the pensioner must be increased by such percentage as equals the overall percentage by which, had the pension been in payment as from the date when the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age until the spouse’s or civil partner’s death, that weekly rate would have increased during that period by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act (annual uprating of benefits).
@ref s 51(11) and (12) (src:1634-1637)
GIVEN `the spouse or civil partner attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the spouse or civil partner died after attaining pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the overall percentage by which the weekly rate would have increased by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 51(12) the weekly rate of the additional pension after the increase in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the spouse or civil partner attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016` AND `the spouse or civil partner died after attaining pensionable age`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the overall percentage by which the weekly rate would have increased by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the orders under section 150 are not among the sources
        WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST (`the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds` TIMES (1 PLUS (percentage DIVIDED BY 100)))
    ELSE JUST `the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds`  -- unmodified, not a "no": subsection (12) increases the amount "in the case of" a pensioner whose spouse or civil partner (a) attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016 and (b) died after attaining it (marginal reading (c) in NOTES.md)

§§ `Section 51ZA: special provision for married person whose spouse changed gender`

-- (1): section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled to a Category B retirement pension in a case where
-- (a) her spouse is a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and (b) the marriage subsisted before
-- the certificate was issued.
-- src:1639 | (1) Section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled to a Category B retirement pension under that section in a case where—
-- src:1640 | (a) her spouse is a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004, and
-- src:1641 | (b) the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued.
@ref s 51ZA(1) (src:1639-1641)
GIVEN woman IS A Person
      `her spouse is a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` MEANS
    woman's `sex` EQUALS Woman
    AND `her spouse is a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004`
    AND `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): outside "a case where (a) ... and (b) ..." the section does not lift the bar, and section 48A(2)(b) stands by its own terms

-- (2): section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled in a case where (a) her former spouse was, at the
-- time the marriage was dissolved, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and (b) the marriage
-- subsisted before the certificate was issued.
-- src:1642 | (2) Section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled to a Category B retirement pension under that section in a case where—
-- src:1643 | (a) her former spouse was, at the time the marriage was dissolved, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004, and
-- src:1644 | (b) the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued.
@ref s 51ZA(2) (src:1642-1644)
GIVEN woman IS A Person
      `her former spouse was at the time the marriage was dissolved a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` MEANS
    woman's `sex` EQUALS Woman
    AND `her former spouse was at the time the marriage was dissolved a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004`
    AND `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): outside "a case where (a) ... and (b) ..." the section does not lift the bar, and section 48AA(2)(b) stands by its own terms

-- (3): section 48B(1ZA)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled in a case where (a) her dead spouse was, at the
-- time of death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and (b) the marriage subsisted before the
-- certificate was issued; and in such a case the reference in section 48B(1ZB)(a)(ii) to the spouse having attained
-- pensionable age before 6 April 2010 is read as a reference to the spouse having been born before 6 April 1945
-- (that reading is applied by `s 48B(1ZB)` in ssc3-d-s47-s48c.l4, which takes this answer as an input).
-- src:1645 | (3) Section 48B(1ZA)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled to a Category B retirement pension under that section in a case where—
-- src:1646 | (a) her dead spouse was, at the time of death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004, and
-- src:1647 | (b) the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued,
-- src:1648 | and in such a case the reference in section 48B(1ZB)(a)(ii) to the spouse having attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010 is to be read as a reference to the spouse having been born before 6 April 1945.
@ref s 51ZA(3) (src:1645-1648)
GIVEN woman IS A Person
      `her dead spouse was at the time of death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` MEANS
    woman's `sex` EQUALS Woman
    AND `her dead spouse was at the time of death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004`
    AND `the marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): outside "a case where (a) ... and (b) ..." the section does not lift the bar and does not change the reading, and section 48B(1ZA)(b) and (1ZB)(a)(ii) stand by their own terms

§§ `Section 51A: special provision for married people`

-- (1): this section has effect where, apart from section 43(1), a married person or civil partner would be entitled both
-- (a) to a Category A retirement pension and (b) to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the other party's contributions.
-- src:1653 | (1) This section has effect where, apart from section 43(1) above, a married person or civil partner would be entitled both—
-- src:1654 | (a) to a Category A retirement pension, and
-- src:1655 | (b) to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership.
@ref s 51A(1) (src:1653-1655)
GIVEN `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51A(1) this section has effect` MEANS
    `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension`
    AND `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section has effect where" both hold

-- (3): this section does not apply where both parties to the marriage attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979.
-- src:1659 | (3) This section does not apply in any case where both parties to the marriage attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979
@ref s 51A(3) (src:1659)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `the other party` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51A(3) this section does not apply` MEANS
    person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1979)
    AND `the other party`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1979)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section does not apply in any case where both parties to the marriage attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979"

-- (2): if by reason of a deficiency of contributions the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short
-- of the weekly rate specified in paragraph 5 of Part I of Schedule 4, it is increased by the lesser of the shortfall and
-- the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension. The Schedule 4 figure arrives as an input.
-- src:1656 | (2) If by reason of a deficiency of contributions the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short of the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 5, that basic pension shall be increased by the lesser of—
-- src:1657 | (a) the amount of the shortfall, or
-- src:1658 | (b) the amount of the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension.
@ref s 51A(2) (src:1656-1658)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `the other party` IS A Person
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short by reason of a deficiency of contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt I para 5 the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 51A(3) this section does not apply` person `the other party`
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in any case where both parties to the marriage attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979"
        IF NOT (`s 51A(1) this section has effect` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership`)
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section has effect where" both entitlements arise
        IF NOT `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short by reason of a deficiency of contributions`
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If by reason of a deficiency of contributions the basic pension ... falls short" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `sch 4 pt I para 5 the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension in pounds`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 5 is not among the sources
            WHEN JUST full THEN
                IF `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` LESS THAN full
                THEN JUST (min (full MINUS `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds`) `the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds`)
                ELSE JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "falls short of the weekly rate" -- a basic pension that does not fall short is not increased (marginal reading (a))

§§ `Section 52: special provision for surviving spouses`

-- (1): this section has effect where, apart from section 43(1), a person would be entitled both (a) to a Category A
-- retirement pension and (b) to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil
-- partner who has died.
-- src:1661 | (1) This section has effect where, apart from section 43(1) above, a person would be entitled both—
-- src:1662 | (a) to a Category A retirement pension; and
-- src:1663 | (b) to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died.
@ref s 52(1) (src:1661-1663)
GIVEN `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(1) this section has effect` MEANS
    `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension`
    AND `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section has effect where" both entitlements arise

-- (4): this section does not apply where the death of the wife or husband occurred before 6 April 1979 and the
-- surviving spouse had attained pensionable age before that date.
-- src:1673 | (4) This section does not apply in any case where the death of the wife or husband, as the case may be, occurred before 6th April 1979 and the surviving spouse had attained pensionable age before that date.
@ref s 52(4) (src:1673)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the surviving spouse` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(4) this section does not apply` MEANS
    `the date of the death` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1979)
    AND `the surviving spouse`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1979)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section does not apply in any case where the death ... occurred before 6th April 1979 and the surviving spouse had attained pensionable age before that date"

-- (2): if by reason of a deficiency of contributions the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short
-- of the full amount (the weekly rate of the basic pension in section 44(4)), it is increased by the lesser of the
-- shortfall and the amount of the basic pension in the rate of the Category B retirement pension.
-- src:1664 | (2) If by reason of a deficiency of contributions the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short of the full amount, that basic pension shall be increased by the lesser of—
-- src:1665 | (a) the amount of the shortfall, or
-- src:1666 | (b) the amount of the basic pension in the rate of the Category B retirement pension,
-- src:1667 | “full amount” meaning for this purpose the sum specified in section 44(4) above as the weekly rate of the basic pension in a Category A retirement pension.
@ref s 52(2) (src:1664-1667)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the surviving spouse` IS A Person
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short by reason of a deficiency of contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the basic pension in the rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 52(4) this section does not apply` `the date of the death` `the surviving spouse`
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in any case where the death of the wife or husband ... occurred before 6th April 1979 and the surviving spouse had attained pensionable age before that date"
        IF NOT (`s 52(1) this section has effect` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died`)
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section has effect where" both entitlements arise
        IF NOT `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short by reason of a deficiency of contributions`
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If by reason of a deficiency of contributions the basic pension ... falls short of the full amount" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 44(4) the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds` FALSE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the full amount is the weekly rate of section 44(4)
            WHEN JUST full THEN
                IF `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` LESS THAN full
                THEN JUST (min (full MINUS `the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds`) `the amount of the basic pension in the rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds`)
                ELSE JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "falls short of the full amount" -- a basic pension that does not fall short is not increased (marginal reading (a))

-- (3A): the references to additional pension in a Category A or Category B retirement pension in (3) do not include any
-- amount of additional pension attributable to units of additional pension.
-- src:1671 | (3A) In subsection (3) the references to additional pension in a Category A or Category B retirement pension do not include any amount of additional pension attributable to units of additional pension.
@ref s 52(3A) (src:1671)
GIVEN `the additional pension in the retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of it attributable to units of additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 52(3A) the additional pension for subsection (3) in pounds` MEANS
    `the additional pension in the retirement pension in pounds` MINUS `the amount of it attributable to units of additional pension in pounds`

-- (3): if the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short of the maximum amount specified in
-- regulations, it is increased by the lesser of the shortfall and the additional pension in the Category B retirement pension.
-- The maximum amount arrives as an input. Both additional pensions are as (3A) leaves them.
-- src:1668 | (3) If the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension falls short of the maximum amount specified in regulations, that additional pension shall be increased by the lesser of—
-- src:1669 | (a) the amount of the shortfall, or
-- src:1670 | (b) the amount of the additional pension in the Category B retirement pension.
@ref s 52(3) (src:1668-1670)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the surviving spouse` IS A Person
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension for subsection (3) in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum amount of additional pension specified in regulations in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the additional pension in the Category B retirement pension for subsection (3) in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 52(4) this section does not apply` `the date of the death` `the surviving spouse`
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in any case where the death of the wife or husband ... occurred before 6th April 1979 and the surviving spouse had attained pensionable age before that date"
        IF NOT (`s 52(1) this section has effect` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died`)
        THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section has effect where" both entitlements arise
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the maximum amount of additional pension specified in regulations in pounds`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the maximum amount specified in regulations" is not among the sources
            WHEN JUST maximum THEN
                IF `the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension for subsection (3) in pounds` LESS THAN maximum
                THEN JUST (min (maximum MINUS `the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension for subsection (3) in pounds`) `the additional pension in the Category B retirement pension for subsection (3) in pounds`)
                ELSE JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the additional pension ... falls short of the maximum amount" -- a pension that does not fall short is not increased (marginal reading (a))

-- (3B): if an amount of additional pension in the Category B retirement pension is attributable to units of additional
-- pension, the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension is increased by that amount (in addition to any
-- increase under (3)).
-- src:1672 | (3B) If an amount of additional pension in the Category B retirement pension is attributable to units of additional pension, the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension is increased by that amount (in addition to any increase under subsection (3)).
@ref s 52(3B) (src:1672)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the surviving spouse` IS A Person
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of additional pension in the Category B retirement pension attributable to units of additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 52(3B) the further increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 52(4) this section does not apply` `the date of the death` `the surviving spouse`
        THEN 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in any case where the death of the wife or husband ... occurred before 6th April 1979 and the surviving spouse had attained pensionable age before that date"
        IF NOT (`s 52(1) this section has effect` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` `apart from section 43(1) the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of a spouse or civil partner who has died`)
        THEN 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "This section has effect where" both entitlements arise
        OTHERWISE `the amount of additional pension in the Category B retirement pension attributable to units of additional pension in pounds`

§§ `Section 55: pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to retirement pension is deferred`

-- (3): a person's entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred if and so long as the person
-- (a) does not become entitled to it by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration
-- Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim), or (b) in consequence of an election under section 54(1) falls to be
-- treated as not having become entitled to it. Two other parts ask this under two names (seams S10 and S37).
-- src:1694 | (3) For the purposes of this Act a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred if and so long as that person—
-- src:1695 | (a) does not become entitled to that pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim), or
-- src:1696 | (b) in consequence of an election under section 54(1), falls to be treated as not having become entitled to that pension,
-- src:1697 | and, in relation to any such pension, “period of deferment” shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 55(3) (src:1694-1697)
GIVEN `the person does not become entitled to the pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in consequence of an election under section 54(1) the person falls to be treated as not having become entitled to the pension` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deferred if and so long as that person" -- (a) or (b) (an "if and so long as" test)
    `ssc3 helper any of`
        (LIST
            `the person does not become entitled to the pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim)`
          , `in consequence of an election under section 54(1) the person falls to be treated as not having become entitled to the pension`)

-- (3), under the second name that seam S37 asks it by.
GIVEN `the person does not become entitled to the pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in consequence of an election under section 54(1) the person falls to be treated as not having become entitled to the pension` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55(3) the pension is deferred` MEANS
    `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred`
        `the person does not become entitled to the pension by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to benefit dependent on claim)`
        `in consequence of an election under section 54(1) the person falls to be treated as not having become entitled to the pension`

-- (1): where a person's entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred, Schedule 5 has effect.
-- src:1685 | (1) Where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred, Schedule 5 to this Act has effect.
@ref s 55(1) (src:1685)
GIVEN `the entitlement to the pension is deferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55(1) Schedule 5 has effect` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement to the pension is deferred` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Schedule 5 "has effect" where entitlement is deferred; the section does not say it has no effect otherwise
